WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.479
Model provenance means understanding where a model came from, who created it, how it was trained or fine-tuned, and whether it is appropriate for the intended use.

2
00:00:09.479 --> 00:00:15.914
Teams should be cautious when downloading or integrating models from unknown or poorly documented sources.

3
00:00:15.914 --> 00:00:22.839
Model artifacts can raise licensing, security, performance, privacy, and reliability concerns.

4
00:00:22.839 --> 00:00:27.080
Model selection should involve more than checking whether a demo looks impressive.

5
00:00:27.080 --> 00:00:34.174
Teams need to understand limitations, intended use, maintenance, update practices, and evaluation results.

6
00:00:34.174 --> 00:00:42.495
Provenance helps teams decide whether a model belongs in a product, requires additional review, or should be limited to experimentation.
